From 74ca1998141ac7eb3360c00b2cb35ce83cd132b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:18:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(post): wire-iso writes each dimension word with a
 decimal point

Many wire controls read a number without a decimal point in their
least input unit (0.001 mm), so X5 moved 5 um there, not 5 mm. The
wire-iso post now writes every X, Y, U, V, I, J and taper angle word
with its point (X5., Y0., U0., A3.), as the Sodick post already does.
Comment text keeps its plain numbers. The eight wire-iso goldens move
by the point only; wire_iso_decimal pins the rule over each golden.

Fixes #3206

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
